 \\cdot 4} = \\frac{7 \\pm \\sqrt{49 - 32}}{8} = \\frac{7 \\pm \\sqrt{17}}{8}\\]\nSo the roots are:\n\\[x_3 = \\frac{7 + \\sqrt{17}}{8}, \\quad x_4 = \\frac{7 - \\sqrt{17}}{8}\\]\n\n### Step 3: Find the product of the roots\nThe product of the roots of the equation \\((2x^2 - 5x + 1)(4x^2 - 7x + 2) = 0\\) is the product of the roots of each quadratic factor. By Vieta's formulas, the product of the roots of the quadratic equation \\(ax^2 + bx + c = 0\\) is given by \\(\\frac{c}{a}\\).\n\nFor \\(2x^2 - 5x + 1 = 0\\), the product of the roots is:\n\\[\\frac{1}{2}\\]\n\nFor \\(4x^2 - 7x + 2 = 0\\), the product of the roots is:\n\\[\\frac{2}{4} = \\frac{1}{2}\\]\n\nThe product of all four roots is:\n\\[\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) \\times \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right) = \\frac{1}{4}\\]\n\n### Step 4: Interpret the product of the roots as the area of the rectangle\nThe product of the roots represents the area of the rectangle when the roots represent the lengths of the sides. Therefore, the area of the rectangle is:\n\\[\\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}\\]\n\nFind } \\frac{x}{y} \\text{ where } \\frac{x}{y} = -\\frac{10}{7} - \\frac{8i}{7}.\\text{\n\nTo find \\(\\frac{x}{y}\\) where \\(x = -\\frac{10}{7} - \\frac{8i}{7}\\) and \\(y = -\\frac{10}{7} + \\frac{8i}{7}\\), we start by expressing \\(\\frac{x}{y}\\) in terms of a complex number.\n\nFirst, let's denote:\n\\[ x = -\\frac{10}{7} - \\frac{8i}{7} \\]\n\\[ y = -\\frac{10}{7} + \\frac{8i}{7} \\]\n\nWe need to find \\(\\frac{x}{y}\\). To do this, we will multiply the numerator and the denominator by the complex conjugate of the denominator \\(y\\), which is \\(-\\frac{10}{7} - \\frac{8i}{7}\\).\n\nThe expression becomes:\n\\[ \\frac{x}{y} = \\frac{-\\frac{10}{7} - \\frac{8i}{7}}{-\\frac{10}{7} + \\frac{8i}{7}} \\]\n\nTo simplify the denominator, we multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\\[ \\frac{-\\frac{10}{7} - \\frac{8i}{7}}{-\\frac{10}{7} + \\frac{8i}{7}} \\cdot \\frac{-\\frac{10}{7} - \\