      "text": "We begin by solving the first equation for $x$. Subtracting $7$ from both sides, we get $2x=-4$. Dividing both sides by $2$, we have $x=-2$.\n\nNow we substitute this value of $x$ into the second equation, $bx-10=-2$, to find the value of $b$.\n\n\\[b(-2)-10=-2\\]\n\n\\[ \\rightarrow -2b-10=-2\\]\n\n\\[ \\rightarrow -2b=-8\\]\n\nSince $b$ is a coefficient and we need to isolate $b$, we divide both sides by $-2$:\n\n\\[b=\\frac{8}{2}\\]\n\nSince $b=\\frac{8}{2}=4$\n\nHence, the value of $b$ is \\boxed{4}.",
